	<body>
		<outline text="/scripting.com/code/wpidentity/">
			<outline text="worknotes.md">
				<outline text="#### 10/11/26; 12:21:54 PM by DW -- v0.5.43">
					<outline text="In startMail, skip mail.start  when there are no SMTP settings, leaving the host app’s setup in place. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Needed for feedland.com, which can handle identity by email or wordpress.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 6/2/26; 7:45:58 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Commented the &quot;missing functionality&quot; section of the history, what was listed there is no longer missing. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/18/26; 10:42:58 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Added links to demo apps up front in the main readme. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/13/26; 7:44:46 AM by DW -- v0.5.41">
					<outline text="addPost and updatePost pass the contentType to processPostText and only does the processing if it's markdown.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="new config -- flUseGlossary, default false">
						<outline text="* we haven't documented the glossary feature, and it slows down an already too-slow process">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* we will put it in for real at some point, until then, it's disabled">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/11/26; 12:29:00 PM by DW -- v0.5.39">
					<outline text="getSourceFiles and deleteSourceFiles, needed for wpEditorDemo. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/28/26; 11:03:08 AM by DW">
					<outline text="New function saveFeed. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Call via api2.js as myWordpress.saveFeed (idSite).">
					</outline>
					<outline text="We now do rss building here. Used to be in WordLand.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Added turndown as a dependency.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/16/26; 11:06:01 AM by DW">
					<outline text="new endpoint, getWordlandDraft. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/13/26; 9:17:34 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In convertPost, we normalize guids that come from the API to agree with the format for guids in WordPress feeds. Wrote it up &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Automattic/wp-calypso/issues/109266&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/9/26; 5:33:34 PM by DW">
					<outline text="In addPost, if the jsontext obj has an inReplyTo object, we copy it into the draft we return.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/1/26; 10:20:24 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In getEdges, having no edges is not an error, just return an empty array.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 1/31/26; 10:04:41 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Added a note to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/scripting/wpIdentity/blob/main/docs/storage.md#how-it-works&quot;&gt;storage docs page&lt;/a&gt;, explaining that most files we serve are private, but there are examples of files we manage that are public. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 1/29/26; 10:01:56 AM by DW -- v0.5.32">
					<outline text="typo, changed wordpressggetedges to wordpressgetedges.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="when i updated to v0.5.31 the getEdges call stopped working. ">
						<outline text="* i got the url and tried to open it in the browser">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* it hung there, eventually with an error to localhost">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* i was talking to wordland.dev">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* so i added debugging code, and everything worked perfectly">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* the only diff is that it was running wpidentity from the npm install command and the new version with debugging code came through a testing update, manually copying to the right location in wpIdentity folder">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* i expect this to surface again at some point, so wanted to leave a note here">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="now I'm going to comment the debugging code, create v0.5.32, and repeat the update process on the wordland.dev server (maine)">
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 1/28/26; 10:18:30 AM by DW -- v0.5.31">
					<outline text="getEdges now includes the number of edges pointing to each of the edges we return. allows me to parenthetically include how many replies there are for each reply.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="added to the definition of the edges table in the docs">
						<outline text="* key edgesToPost (idDestSite, idDestPost)">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="ran this in mysql">
						<outline text="* create index edgesToPost on edges (idDestSite, idDestPost);">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/15/25; 9:56:20 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In getEdges, return the array sorted by whenCreated.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/5/25; 12:07:39 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Edges are in, and working. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="In getEdges in api2.js, added reverse chronologic sort to the array we return.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/2/25; 9:21:41 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Slowly and carefully adding mail back in. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Getting started with edges.">
						<outline text="create table edges (">
							<outline text="id int auto_increment primary key,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idSourceSite int not null,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idSourcePost int not null,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idDestSite int not null,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idDestPost int not null,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="sourceAuthor varchar (255)  not null default'',">
							</outline>
							<outline text="destAuthor  varchar (255)  not null default'',">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated datetime not null default current_timestamp, ">
							</outline>
							<outline text="approved boolean default false,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="unique key sourceDest (idSourceSite, idSourcePost, idDestSite, idDestPost)">
							</outline>
							<outline text=");">
							</outline>
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/1/25; 9:13:45 AM by DW -- v0.5.28">
					<outline text="Working on discourse features. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="New function -- getPostAuthorInfo.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="New function -- getWordlandPrefs, takes a username and returns their prefs. ">
						<outline text="* this allows us to find out if they've enabled notification on replies.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* that means that in order to be part of this system they must have used this WordLand once to set that up.">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="New function -- testNotification -- leaving it in there for now, not sure how we're going to interface from wpIdentity to where ever the linkage between posts is stored. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I started to include davemail here, but that causes all the problems that adding a feature to reallysimple caused. It's probably better to make it a separate app, connected by HTTP.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/28/25; 11:48:22 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Added queriesthatwork.md in docs folder. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/15/25; 9:45:43 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In api2.js, set options.flMarkdownProcess to false by default. The option was created before we established that the server would only store markdown text for posts. To set it true would probably break that, so it made no sense for it to default to false. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/31/25; 6:44:10 AM by DW -- v0.5.27">
					<outline text="Another breaking change from the new version of wpcom package. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="They changed the way it interfaces, so the way we call it here no longer works.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="We could easily convert to the new way, but I decided not to, and to require the previous version, 5.4.2, which we developed around.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Since there have been two breaking changes, that says to me the probability of a third is pretty high. ;-)">
					</outline>
					<outline text="And with this change we can now comment out the requirement of babel in package.json.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/27/25; 9:55:18 AM by DW -- v0.5.26">
					<outline text="Trying to install the updated feedland app on feedland.org, and believe there's a bug in the new release of wpcom package, it uses but does not include in its dependencies the babel runtime. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I'm working around it by adding a dependency on babel runtime here, bumping the version number of wpidentity, and requiring at least that version in feedlandserver (which is feedland package), ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I got help from claude.ai in piecing this together. I don't like having to work at this level. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/22/25; 10:50:57 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Finished basic cleanup of api2.js at a source level. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Updated the home page of the repo to make it more clear that it is much more than identity. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/18/25; 10:13:11 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Fixed an infinite loop at startup if you didn't have your userinfo in wordpressmemory. ">
						<outline text="* This was one of the changes in the big new version, and it hadn't gotten tested, but it's one of hte pieces of code that's shared between all versions of wordland, so it broke users of the old version. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* Have to get this part straightend out, there has to be a place to store the old frozen version so we can't accidentally break it like this. But this problem should be fixed now. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="There were two functions called getUserInfo. I changed the lower-level one to getUserInfoFromServer.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/5/25; 9:58:55 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Released v0.5.25 so it can be used by FeedLand. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/29/25; 5:26:07 PM by DW">
					<outline text="In the API, getFeedUrl, if username is undefined, use the current user's name.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/18/25; 8:56:52 PM by DW">
					<outline text="New api endpoint -- getSiteInfoSync. Gets the info about the site from a local in-memory cache. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/17/25; 11:39:28 AM by DW">
					<outline text="New endpoint -- &lt;s&gt;getDraftFromUrl&lt;/s&gt;. ">
						<outline text="On second thought decided to do it another way, in the client app, where we have a list of all the drafts that the user can edit via another call. Keep remembering that text is small, and we can afford to transmit an array with lots of elements in it. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/5/25; 10:37:13 AM by DW">
					<outline text="New endpoint -- getrangeofdraftsforuser, calls new function -- getRangeOfDraftsForUser.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 7/5/25; 10:11:12 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Add metadata to post, basically send through a few bits of info we have in the WordLand's draft object. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The values we add to the metadata for the post:">
						<outline text="* wordland_apiVersion: the version number of the metadata we include, starting with 0.4.0 today.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* wordland_linksTo: the value of the item-level &amp;lt;link&gt; element in WordLand's RSS feed for the site, if there is one, the empty string if not. It's used in linkblog posts. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* wordland_idDraft: a unique id for this post in WordLand's database. It is only unique to this instance of the server. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* wordland_markdowntext: WordLand stores the post in Markdown format. We like to include it along with the rendered text whenever we can, encouraging broader use of Markdown. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* wordland_title: the title of the post, the empty string if the post doesn't have a title.">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="There are limits to where this works, I will try to find out exactly where they are. ;-)">
					</outline>
					<outline text="A &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/scripting/wpIdentity/issues/6&quot;&gt;place&lt;/a&gt; for questions and comments.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/11/25; 11:00:38 AM by DW">
					<outline text="A new endpoint to update a category: updateSiteCategory.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/4/25; 8:58:10 AM by DW">
					<outline text="in api2.js">
						<outline text="* When we startup do an initial websocket checkConnection after 1/10th second. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* Then we check every 10 seconds.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* I didn't like the lag at startup, having to wait 10 secs before we start the connection.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* All the complexity is for when it doesn't work. What about when it does?">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/1/25; 4:43:06 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Rewrote wsConnectUserToServer in api2.js. It was retrying a failed connection once a second and never terminates. Now it tries once every ten seconds and gives up after 100 tries. I think this is still pretty generous and the number of tries could be reduced without giving up anything. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/28/25; 9:02:20 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Rewrote the websocket code to use the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.npmjs.com/package/ws&quot;&gt;ws package&lt;/a&gt; instead of the &quot;nodejs-websocket&quot;. As promised by all my chatbot ai friends, it fixed a big problem, and promises to work better with everything. Esp important for networking software. ;-)">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Fixed a problem in convertSite where the server would crash if it was converting a site that was not running on wordpress.com. The problem is that such sites don't contain an options object. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/27/25; 4:57:44 PM by DW">
					<outline text="In webSocketStartup we watch for errors and report them.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/24/25; 5:45:59 PM by DW">
					<outline text="getSiteCategories now paginates, so if you have 300+ categories, we can handle it. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/26/25; 9:49:16 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In uploadImage, check for idSite == &quot;undefined&quot; -- return an error, don't try to upload. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="But it's even worse than it appears. In api2.js, there is new code for my codebase for doing a POST using jQuery. And it hadn't been tested with errors returned from a POST operation. The bug in the new code was that it always reported &quot;error&quot; even though the server had returned a more meaningful message. It took me a while to look at the client. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/24/25; 5:53:10 PM by DW">
					<outline text="We were adding posts and updating posts via HTTP GET and we have to use POST. Hit the limit today on a post I was updating. Made the switch. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/17/25; 12:31:15 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Add urlAvatar, urlProfile to the user info record we return via the api.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/15/25 by DW">
					<outline text="New category endpoints -- wordpressaddcategory, wordpressdeletecategory.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/14/25; 10:27:39 AM by DW">
					<outline text="config.homePagetable lets you add macros to the home page for the site being served through the home page. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/12/25; 10:07:45 AM by DW">
					<outline text="getUsername, as exported on the 10th, doesn't work -- and I never figured out why. instead i created a clone of callWithUsername that can be called by an app that includes wpIdentity, just as it can call it in its http-handling function. remarkably, it does work. i can now move on.  ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/10/25; 3:28:48 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Exporting getUsername function, it's needed in writersweb. It could have worked with getUserInfo, which is already exported, but we have a cache on getUsername, and rather than replicate the functionality at a higher level, it's best to export it.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/9/25; 1:00:40 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Update in api2.js. this.getUserInfo assumed that the server had already been called to ask for it, and cached it in wordpressMemory, and that's true in WordLand, but not true in a new app I'm working on. So we have to account for that possibility, and be ready to call the server if it isn't initialized. Fairly sure there's no chance of breakage, because we're just replacing undefined with actual data. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/7/25; 4:18:02 PM by DW">
					<outline text="I want to be able to bake wpidentity into an app, starting with writersweb. ">
						<outline text="1. I will need to call it's httpRequest handler, which is exported, so that's cool.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="2. I will need to be able to get information about a user, providing a token and getting back a struct. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Both these functions are already exported. Hmm. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/26/25; 9:49:12 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Adding a users table. I want to be able to gather metadata, right now I want to know what browsers people are using, so I know how important it is to get it working in each browser. Apparently there are problems in some versions of Safari, but I only have gotten one report. I need to see what's actually going on, and to have a way to gather other data. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="See countUserHit function.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The users table is documented on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/scripting/wpIdentity/blob/main/docs/storage.md&quot;&gt;docs/storage.md page&lt;/a&gt;.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/24/25; 9:26:16 AM by DW">
					<outline text="I want separate events for addPost and updatePost operations. ">
						<outline text="* Previously we were using &quot;publish&quot; for both events. So instead of calling both &quot;publish&quot; we'll just use the names of the functions that implement them.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* Also want the title of the post to be included with both events. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/23/25; 12:38:27 PM by DW">
					<outline text="We now log publish operations. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 2/22/25; 9:08:07 AM by DW">
					<outline text="In readUserFile, we need to send a clear message back to the caller if the file they're looking for simply doesn't exist. That is not actually an error here, it happens with bookmarks.opml the first time a user signs on to WordLand. The change is in readUserFile.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 1/24/25; 8:36:53 AM by DW">
					<outline text="If a user has a deleted WordPress website, convertSite will crash, trying to create a data structure for it. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Changes in getUserSites and convertSite. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/23/24; 5:22:22 PM by DW">
					<outline text="New call -- wordpressgettopusers, returns an array of the top users ranked by number of times their WordLand prefs.json file has been read, which happens when you first load the app. It doesn't measure activity, ie editing and publishing. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/23/24; 12:07:10 PM by DW">
					<outline text="The demo app was broken in several ways. It now works properly.">
						<outline text="* Setting serverAddress and urlChatLogSocket correctly at startup, don't depend on defaults in api2.js.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* logOffWordpress was missing.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* viewing the site list was broken because we weren't waiting for the site list to load in myWordpress.startup. Fixed it by reading the site list from the server when displaying the site list. I understand why I didn't want it to wait at startup, it's not something WordLand needs to display until the user asks to see the site list.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* startTestPrefs call was commented out, uncommented, set number of tests to 5 instead of 60. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* There was a problem in saving prefs, something we had fixed in WordLand but the update had not made it into the demo app. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Hopefully from this point forward there will be no more breakage. We've got a good debugged app, WordLand, and it has to remain unbroken from here-out, so that bodes well, we hope, ymmv, ianal, mmlm. :-)">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 12/21/24; 11:47:17 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Add a log table using my new &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/scripting/sqlLog&quot;&gt;sqlLog&lt;/a&gt; package.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Added config.flLogInstalled, default false. If false we won't call the log package, it should be false if you haven't created a log table in your sql database.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Now let's add some logging code">
						<outline text="* on startup, log config.urlServer">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* on websocket connect, log username">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Initially I had logging in writeWholeFile but decided this was too much (for now). ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="May also want to add one for every http request, makes more sense, would require a slight rewrite so we could log the username making the request. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/18/24; 11:34:35 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Turned off config.flConvertImagesToGutenberg.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="From the GitHub thread, there's a little bit left to do, but they're going to try to account for images in plain HTML, so let's see how that goes. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Basically we have to get the image id to agree with WordPress's idea of what its ID is. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Really have to find and read the docs to be sure I understand how it should work.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/18/24; 10:23:32 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Read authorizedAccounts every minute from the file.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="New config value -- config.authorizedAccountsPath.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Read the file it points to once a minute, if it exists, we replace config.authorizedAccounts with the JSON structure in the file.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Makes it so you don't have to reboot to add an authorized user, just edit the contents of the file.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="If there's an error parsing the file, we display the error on the console, so if you make a mistake you see it in the log right away.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Look in readAuthorizedAccounts.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/13/24; 8:32:46 AM by DW">
					<outline text="It took three full days to get uploading images to work. A lot of trial and error and guesswork, but the code works now, and today I'm going to clean it up and move on to other things, hopefully.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Note that because we also provide an API that runs in the browser, no one will have to go through this to get functional code, the problem is solved at least for this context. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/10/24; 12:29:58 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Uploading images.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 11/1/24; 10:35:37 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Added support for the nextPrevArray used to implement the arrows in WordLand. See getNextPrevArray.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Released v0.5.5.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/31/24; 7:03:56 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Increase the default config.maxCtDrafts to 1000. Previously it was 100. I'm hitting that limit when I rebuild the Bookmarks menu or backup my drafts. I don't know if we can have a limit, unless we have a limit of drafts for non-paying users. That comes later. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Also changed the default value for options.maxCtUserDraftFiles in api2.j to 1000 to agree. This is passed as a parameter to the server. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/26/24; 9:15:57 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Fixed a startup problem for new users. In getRecentUserDrafts we were getting the most recent drafts for all users, but we must restrict it to the user. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/24/24; 9:19:50 AM by DW">
					<outline text="whitelist -- so we can start testing with a limited group of users.">
						<outline text="* two new config values: config.flUseWhitelist, a boolean default false, authorizedAccounts, an array of usernames who are authorized, default empty array.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* first version, we just add a new api call that allows you to find out if the user is whitelisted. it returns true if the whitelist is not enabled, otherwise search the authorizedAccounts list.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* core function isUserWhitelisted, also in the api2.js.">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/21/24; 10:04:54 AM by DW">
					<outline text="More categories work.">
						<outline text="* We weren't transmitting the categories back to wordpress when creating or updating a wordpress post. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* When asked for a list of categories for a site, do not include &quot;uncategorized.&quot; It's not something the user can choose, nor should they be concerned about it. Not sure what they intended us to do here, but we have to work around it in every instance, so we might as well cut it out at the beginning. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/20/24; 10:38:13 AM by DW">
					<outline text="adding support for categories.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="convertCategory converts a category from WP format to our API's format.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/17/24; 12:30:49 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Fixed a bug in readDraft, it would crash if the draft didn't exist. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/12/24; 10:06:11 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Going to start posting worknotes here again.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="How to debug this locally. This is what I always forget how to do so I'm documenting it somewhere I think I'll look for the info. If only I could tell ChatGPT to remember this for me. Someday soon of course. ;-) ">
						<outline text="1. Create localStorage.wordpressMemory in the JS debugger on the client machine you're using for testing.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="2. One value must be set -- accessToken -- which you should copy from a client system you're using to access the app.">
							<outline text="* localStorage.wordpressMemory = {&quot;accessToken&quot;: &quot;asdfasdfasdfsf&quot;}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="3. You should start with a working config.json from the server, and modify it to correspond to the local equivalents. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Changing type of &lt;i&gt;filecontents&lt;/i&gt; column from text to longtext. ">
						<outline text="* alter table wpstorage modify column filecontents longtext;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* one of the RSS feeds we generate got too big for a text, ie 64K.">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/25/24; 10:36:42 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Added websockets support and goodnight kisses. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/17/24; 4:55:01 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Added a whenPublished property to the struct returned by addPost and updatePost. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/13/24; 9:38:56 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Changed the name of the project from wordpressIdentity to wpIdentity, so it agrees with the name of the NPM package. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Fixed a bug in the glossary code, we were failing if there is no glossary.json file for the user. But it's okay to not have a glossary.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/12/24; 9:02:36 AM by DW">
					<outline text="new entrypoint -- writeUniqueFile, explained in a comment at the head of the function in source.opml">
						<outline text="writeWholeFile is the general-purpose routine, this is for files that can only have one instance per path/type/etc">
						</outline>
						<outline text="examples include the user's prefs.json file for a specific app, or the user's glossary.json file. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="these files are a lot simpler to work with than the draft.json files.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="we could manage these files ourselves at a higher level, but that would mean we would have to remember the id of the glossary.json file, in order to save it.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="it's simpler to just provide a new entrypoint for these files that finds the id before writing it, the info is after all, in the database. ;-)">
						</outline>
						<outline text="this could be done on the client, but that means two round trips for the data. this is a little more efficient. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/10/24; 8:53:59 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Adding an &quot;id&quot; column to the database, and changing the queries accordingly.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I believe things will work much better with this approach, basically one row in the database can transition from being a draft to being published without moving. It'll keep the same id. That means you will be able to have more than one unpublished draft. I expect there will be other flexibilities. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The id is the key.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 5/9/24; 11:01:19 AM by DW">
					<outline text="I finally got to the bottom of the problem with http post returning. I'm going to fix it, and probably should eventually visit all the code that uses davehttp, because I have replicated the problem far and wide.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="First, the code I use to call the server uses jQuery in such a way that errors are not reported. If we were seeing the errors we would have been able to find this much more quickly. I'm fixed it in api2.js here. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Second, the server returns the wrong type in returnData in wpidentity.js. It was returning &quot;application/javascript&quot; and should have been returning &quot;text/json&quot;.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/30/24; 10:43:14 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Add param to getRecentUserDrafts to let the caller restrict returns to a specific site. Useful for building feeds. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="If config.flServePublicUserFiles is true, we will serve files from user storage database.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/29/24; 12:12:53 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Update: Changed the way this works, the RSS is generated in the app, and we keep it here in user storage. Eventually public files will be availble via HTTP.">
						<outline text="* Start work on RSS feed for each user.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* My feed would be at https://word.social/feed?username=scripting">
						</outline>
						<outline text="* I checked that FeedLand doesn't have a call for /feed. If it did, we would consume it before it saw it. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/27/24; 10:02:23 AM by DW">
					<outline text="New call --  /wordpressgetrecentuserdrafts.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/26/24; 10:06:14 AM by DW">
					<outline text="The problem with POST was that it works, but we're not getting any returned data. For the application we have right now that's not a deal-stopper. But it will have to be fixed. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="See note in WORD worknotes for today for explanation with glossary.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/18/24; 5:29:13 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Markdown processing as we save to WordPress. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Look in processPostText.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/15/24; 12:05:13 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Process emoji shortcodes. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/13/24; 1:41:39 PM by DW">
					<outline text="By handling &quot;/&quot; in our handleHttpRequest function, we broke FeedLand.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I completely forgot that FeedLand includes this package, and that all HTTP requests go through it first, before anyone else gets it.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="In that context it was meant to only handle authorization events, it certainly wasn't meant to handle requests for the home page.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Imagine my surprise when I went to feedland.social and was greeted by the home page text of an app that is not released. Oy.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="So what's the fix? ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The first thing to do is a new release with the code that handles &quot;/&quot; commented out. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Now the fix the other way --">
						<outline text="take the default values of urlServer and urlServerHomePageSource out of config, in wpidentity.js, below">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if you want us to handle &quot;/&quot; for the app, set urlServerHomePageSource in your config.json file for your app">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Renamed these">
						<outline text="deletefile ==&gt; wordpressdeletefile">
						</outline>
						<outline text="readwholefile ==&gt; wordpressreadwholefile">
						</outline>
						<outline text="writewholefile ==&gt; wordpresswritewholefile">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 4/12/24; 12:12:29 PM by DW">
					<outline text="#### Put the API into a wrapper, so it's easy to spot the WordPress calls in client code. ">
						<outline text="Left the original not-wrapped api file in place, it's used in FeedLand and possibly other places.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="The new api is in api2.js. Yes, I hate that too, but I don't see another way to do it. ;-)">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="#### Got wpidentity.scripting.com running again. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="#### Wrote code for storage">
						<outline text="The demo app maintains a file for each user called demo/prefs.json.">
						</outline>
						<outline text="Just three values in it, a count, a date, and a slogan. Updated every minute. ">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/28/24; 11:36:57 AM by DW">
					<outline text="#### re writeUserDataFile below..">
						<outline text="I couldn't get anything back from the server via POST, so I'm trying GET. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="It worked. I've been over it on both ends, can't see any difference between it and daveappserver which is what we use in feedland and drummer. ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="So I'm just going to continue with calling GET, and trust that the next person to pass this way will figure out what I did wrong. ;-)">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/25/24; 10:08:19 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Add a cache for usernames.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/24/24; 10:55:17 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Moved these notes to docs/storage.md.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 3/23/24; 7:30:58 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Export getUserInfo, which takes an accessToken and calls back with user info.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 10/31/23; 10:25:25 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Allow the caller to handle wordpress login.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/14/23; 8:28:29 AM by DW">
					<outline text="I wanted to set categories for posts via addPost and updatePost, but found the categories have to already exist before using them, it's not as low-tech as I imagined. So for now we'll have to punt on setting categories through these calls.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/13/23; 12:56:32 PM by DW">
					<outline text="We now summarize the various types: site, post, user, mediaobject, etc to a simpler package as we have done with other apps.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Now we have a proper foundation to build on for scripting in Drummer. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/11/23; 12:05:47 PM by DW">
					<outline text="When calling back to the app, instead of calling the parameter accesstoken, call it wordpressaccesstoken, to distinguish it from other apps, such as github. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/10/23; 1:02:07 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Getting ready to include this in daveappserver. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The HTTP requests should all have &quot;wordpress&quot; in their names. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Should be able to get by with changes only in this project, because the api.js code is here. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/5/23; 10:26:37 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Turned into a package so I can include it in other apps, probably FeedLand and Drummer.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Rewrite the readme.md file for this repo to put the whole thing to bed and get ready for the next thing.">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/5/23; 9:25:58 AM by DW">
					<outline text="New functions to delete a post and get the user's subscriptions. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/4/23; 5:33:32 PM by DW">
					<outline text="If you pass a &lt;i&gt;urlapphomepage&lt;/i&gt; parameter to the /connect call, we'll redirect back to that url instead of the default.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="This means that one wpidentity server can support lots of apps. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 9/3/23; 10:16:21 AM by DW">
					<outline text="I took a detour to build a &quot;blog browser&quot; based on the client app here, which was not intended to be anything so robust, it's just meant to be example code.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="So I split it off into its own project, and refocused the client app here to its much more humble beginnings. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/29/23; 12:14:59 PM by DW">
					<outline text="More verbs">
						<outline text="testGetSiteInfo (9969399)">
						</outline>
						<outline text="testGetSiteMedialist (9969399)">
						</outline>
						<outline text="testAddPost (9969399) -- this is the biggie of course, and it &lt;a href=&quot;https://unberkeley.wordpress.com/2023/08/29/so-youd-like-a-test-post-2/&quot;&gt;worked&lt;/a&gt; the first time. ;-)">
						</outline>
						<outline text="testUpdatePost (9969399, 4594) -- and this works too, changes the content without touching the title and other properties.">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/28/23; 7:45:13 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Let's add some verbs.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="The docs we need are here.">
						<outline text="https://github.com/Automattic/wp-calypso/tree/trunk/packages/wpcom.js">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="This is how you get the info about a post. Type this into the client console..">
						<outline text="testGetPost (9969399, 4588)">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="The verbs I just implemented --">
						<outline text="getSitePosts (token, params.idsite, httpReturn);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="getSiteUsers (token, params.idsite, httpReturn);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="getPost (token, params.idsite, params.idpost, httpReturn);">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/28/23; 10:59:21 AM by DW">
					<outline text="No server changes. On the client, we now &lt;a href=&quot;https://imgs.scripting.com/2023/08/28/sitelist.png&quot;&gt;display a list&lt;/a&gt; of your sites with creation and modification dates after you sign on. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/27/23; 10:17:33 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Now I &lt;i&gt;really really&lt;/i&gt; have it working. :smile: ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="After getting getUserInfo to work, I thought let's quickly test getting a list of user sites, but that didn't work because i didn't get a powerful enough token. That led me back to the authentication docs, and i don't see anything there about scopes. So now I'm back to zero, I have to find docs. I consulted ChatGPT of course. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="And then I found these docs, which were *exactly* what I needed. ">
						<outline text="https://developer.wordpress.com/docs/oauth2/">
						</outline>
						<outline text="https://github.com/Automattic/wp-calypso/tree/trunk/packages/wpcom.js/docs">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="If you're trying to figure out how the wordpress.com api works, this is the place to start. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Added a new config value -- config.scopes, defaults to &quot;global&quot;. With that I was able to define the /getusersites endpoint. And it works. This is a big part of what I was trying to get to.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Run the &lt;a href=&quot;http://scripting.com/code/wpidentity/client/&quot;&gt;example client&lt;/a&gt; and if you're already signed in, sign out and in again to get the more powerful token and in the JavaScript console enter: ">
						<outline text="&lt;code&gt;testGetUserSites ()&lt;/code&gt;">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="You get a lot of data for that request. In the next iteration I hope to provide a way to browse it. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/26/23; 12:14:10 PM by DW">
					<outline text="Now I &lt;i&gt;really&lt;/i&gt; have it working. :smile: ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="What I didn't know about the last version is that the accessToken was getting mangled by URL-encoding it. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="I hadn't actually used the accessToken until today and when I did, I got an error from wordpress.com saying that it wasn't a valid token. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="After some thought and working it out with ChatGPT (my virtual programming partner, &lt;a href=&quot;https://chat.openai.com/share/7ecef75d-7fb4-475c-940e-7834258da3e5&quot;&gt;transcript included&lt;/a&gt;) I send the token back and forth by base64-ing, and url-safing it, and only doing it via HTTPS. And it works. I got a nice structure of information about me back from the server. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="Next session I'm going to try getting a list of my blogs, and then a list of posts, etc. The model here is the davetwitter package I build all my apps on. Not going to go nearly as far, at least not at first, but enough so that I can do a nice little editor for WordPress writing. ">
					</outline>
					<outline text="To test, go to the &lt;a href=&quot;http://scripting.com/code/wpidentity/client/&quot;&gt;client test page&lt;/a&gt;. Sign in, then open the JavaScript console and type: ">
						<outline text="&lt;code&gt;testGetUserInfo ()&lt;/code&gt;">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="If it worked you should see some info about yourself. If it didn't please report an &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/scripting/wordpressIdentity/issues&quot;&gt;issue&lt;/a&gt;. ">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="#### 8/22/23; 10:21:35 AM by DW">
					<outline text="Started.">
					</outline>
					<outline text="A8C docs are here -- ">
						<outline text="https://developer.wordpress.com/docs/wpcc/">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="A8C examples --">
						<outline text="https://github.com/Automattic/wpcom-connect-examples">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="WPCOM docs --">
						<outline text="https://github.com/Automattic/wp-calypso/tree/trunk/packages/wpcom.js">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="Repo is here --">
						<outline text="https://github.com/scripting/wordpressIdentity">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
			</outline>
			<outline text="package.json">
				<outline text="{">
					<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
						<outline text="10/27/25; 10:02:07 AM by DW">
							<outline text="Added dependency for &quot;@babel/runtime&quot; -- apparently wpcom uses it but does not include it as a dependency.">
							</outline>
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;name&quot;: &quot;wpidentity&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;description&quot;: &quot;Implements OAuth identity, a simple verb set with wordpress.com for Node.js apps, and a storage system for drafts and other user data. It's used in FeedLand for WordPress identity and it's the backend of WordLand.&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;author&quot;: &quot;Dave Winer &lt;dave@scripting.com&gt;&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;version&quot;: &quot;0.5.43&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;license&quot;: &quot;MIT&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;repository&quot;: {">
						<outline text="&quot;type&quot;: &quot;git&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://github.com/scripting/wpidentity.git&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="},">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;main&quot;: &quot;wpidentity.js&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;files&quot;: [">
						<outline text="&quot;wpidentity.js&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="],">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="&quot;dependencies&quot; : {">
						<outline text="&quot;@babel/runtime&quot;: &quot;*&quot;," isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;wpcom&quot;: &quot;5.4.2&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;wpcom&quot;: &quot;*&quot;," isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;request&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;daveutils&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;davehttp&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;daverss&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;davesql&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;davemail&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;sqllog&quot;: &quot;*&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;marked&quot;: &quot;3.0.8&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;node-emoji&quot;: &quot;1.11.0&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;turndown&quot;: &quot;7.2.2&quot;,">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;nodejs-websocket&quot;: &quot;*&quot;" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="&quot;ws&quot;: &quot;*&quot;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
			</outline>
			<outline text="wpidentity.js">
				<outline text="var myProductName = &quot;wpidentity&quot;, myVersion = &quot;0.5.43&quot;; ">
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="exports.start = start; ">
				</outline>
				<outline text="exports.handleHttpRequest = handleHttpRequest; ">
				</outline>
				<outline text="exports.getUserInfo = getUserInfo; //3/23/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="exports.getUsername = getUsername; //3/10/25 by DW" isComment="true">
				</outline>
				<outline text="exports.callWithUsername = callWithUsernameForClient; //3/12/25 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const fs = require (&quot;fs&quot;);">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const utils = require (&quot;daveutils&quot;); ">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const request = require (&quot;request&quot;);">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const davehttp = require (&quot;davehttp&quot;);">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const wpcom = require (&quot;wpcom&quot;); //8/26/23 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const davesql = require (&quot;davesql&quot;); //3/24/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const emoji = require (&quot;node-emoji&quot;);  //4/15/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const marked = require (&quot;marked&quot;);  //4/18/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const rss = require (&quot;daverss&quot;); //4/29/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const websocket = require (&quot;ws&quot;); //4/28/25 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const websocket = require (&quot;nodejs-websocket&quot;); //5/24/24 by DW " isComment="true">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const log = require (&quot;sqllog&quot;); //12/21/24 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const mail = require (&quot;davemail&quot;); //12/2/25 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="const turndown = require (&quot;turndown&quot;); //3/28/26 by DW">
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="var config = { ">
					<outline text="myRandomNumber: utils.random (1, 1000000000),">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlMyHomePage: &quot;http://scripting.com/code/wpidentity/client/&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlRequestToken: &quot;https://public-api.wordpress.com/oauth2/token&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlAuthorize: &quot;https://public-api.wordpress.com/oauth2/authorize&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlAuthenticate: &quot;https://public-api.wordpress.com/oauth2/authenticate&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlRedirect: &quot;http://localhost:1408/callbackFromWordpress&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="scope: &quot;global&quot;, //default -- 8/27/23 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="mysqlVersion: undefined, //3/24/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flStorageEnabled: false, //3/24/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="ctUsernameCacheSecs: 60, //3/25/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="maxCtDrafts: 1000, //4/27/24 by DW &amp; 10/31/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlServerHomePageSource: &quot;http://scripting.com/code/wordsocial/index.html&quot;, //3/25/24 by DW" isComment="true">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlServer: &quot;https://word.social/&quot; //3/25/24 by DW" isComment="true">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flServePublicUserFiles: false, //4/30/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlPublicUserFiles: &quot;https://wordland.social/&quot;, //5/16/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="maxCtFiles: 100, //5/16/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flWebsocketEnabled: true, //5/24/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="websocketPort: 1622,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="urlSocketServer: &quot;wss://wordland.social/&quot;,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flUseWhitelist: false, //10/24/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="authorizedAccounts: new Array (),">
					</outline>
					<outline text="authorizedAccountsPath: &quot;data/authorizedAccounts.json&quot;, //11/18/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flDeleteTempFiles: true, //11/13/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flConvertImagesToGutenberg: false, //11/16/24 by DW &amp; 11/18/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flLogInstalled: false, //12/21/24 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="sysopUsername: undefined, //2/24/25 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="homePagetable: undefined, //3/14/25 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="postMetadataPrefix: &quot;wordland&quot;, //7/5/25 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="maxFeedItems: 25, //3/28/26 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="feedPingUrl: &quot;https://rpc.rsscloud.io/ping&quot;, //3/28/26 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="flUseGlossary: false, //4/13/26 by DW">
					</outline>
					<outline text="};">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="var stats = {">
					<outline text="ctHits: 0,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="whenLastHit: undefined,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="whenFirstHit: undefined,">
					</outline>
					<outline text="userAgents: {">
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="};">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="function base64UrlEncode (theData) {">
					<outline text="var base64 = Buffer.from (theData).toString ('base64');">
					</outline>
					<outline text="return (base64.replace ('+', '-').replace ('/', '_').replace (/=+$/, ''));">
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function base64UrlDecode (theData) {">
					<outline text="theData = theData.replace ('-', '+').replace ('_', '/');">
					</outline>
					<outline text="while (theData.length % 4) {">
						<outline text="theData += '=';">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="return (Buffer.from (theData, 'base64').toString ('utf-8'));">
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function readConfig (f, config, callback) {">
					<outline text="fs.readFile (f, function (err, jsontext) {">
						<outline text="if (!err) {">
							<outline text="try {">
								<outline text="var jstruct = JSON.parse (jsontext);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="for (var x in jstruct) {">
									<outline text="config [x] = jstruct [x];">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="catch (err) {">
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;Error reading &quot; + f);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="callback ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="});">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function addToLog (eventName, err, eventData, callback) { //12/21/24 by DW">
					<outline text="if (config.flLogInstalled) {">
						<outline text="log.addToLog (eventName, err, eventData, callback);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function getUsername (token, callback) { //3/24/24 by DW">
					<outline text="console.log (&quot;getUsername: token == &quot; + token); //3/12/25 by DW" isComment="true">
					</outline>
					<outline text="if (utils.secondsSince (whenLastUsernameCacheStart) &gt; config.ctUsernameCacheSecs) {">
						<outline text="usernameCache = new Object ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="if (usernameCache [token] !== undefined) {">
						<outline text="callback (undefined, usernameCache [token]);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="else {">
						<outline text="getUserInfo (token, function (err, theUser) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const username = theUser.username;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="usernameCache [token] = username;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, username);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function callWithUsernameForClient (theRequest, callback) { //3/12/25 by DW -- special function for apps that include wpidentity">
					<outline text="const params = theRequest.params;">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function returnError (err) {">
						<outline text="theRequest.httpReturn (503, &quot;text/plain&quot;, err.message);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function isUserWhitelisted (token, callback) {">
						<outline text="callback (undefined, true);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function tokenRequired (callback) {">
						<outline text="const token = (params.token === undefined) ? undefined : base64UrlDecode (params.token);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (token === undefined) {">
							<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the info because the user must be logged in.&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="returnError ({message});">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="isUserWhitelisted (token, function (err, flWhitelisted) { //10/24/24 by DW">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="returnError (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="callback (token);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="tokenRequired (function (token) {">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="returnError (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (username);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="});">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="function getMarkdownFromHtml (htmltext) { //3/28/26 by DW">
					<outline text="const myTurndown = new turndown ();">
					</outline>
					<outline text="const markdowntext = myTurndown.turndown (htmltext);">
					</outline>
					<outline text="return (markdowntext);">
					</outline>
					<outline text="}">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="">
				</outline>
				<outline text="//wordpress">
					<outline text="function connectWithWordpress (callback) {" isComment="true">
						<outline text="var params = {">
							<outline text="client_id: config.clientId,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="redirect_uri: config.urlRedirect,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="response_type: &quot;code&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="scope: &quot;global,auth,user,read,posts,follow,activity,likes&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="state: config.myRandomNumber">
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="var apiUrl = config.urlAuthenticate + &quot;?&quot; + utils.buildParamList (params);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="request (apiUrl, function (err, response, body) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;connectWithWordpress: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;connectWithWordpress: body == &quot; + body);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, body);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function requestTokenFromWordpress (theCode, callback) {">
						<outline text="var theRequest = {">
							<outline text="method: &quot;POST&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="url: config.urlRequestToken,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="form: {">
								<outline text="client_id: config.clientId,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="client_secret: config.clientSecret,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="redirect_uri: config.urlRedirect,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="code: theCode,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="scope: config.scope," isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="grant_type: &quot;authorization_code&quot;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="request (theRequest, function (err, response, body) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="try {">
									<outline text="const data = JSON.parse (body);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, data);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="catch (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertDate (theDate) {">
						<outline text="if (theDate === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return (undefined);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="const d = new Date (theDate);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (isNaN (d)) {">
								<outline text="return (undefined);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (d);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertString (theString) {">
						<outline text="if (theString === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return (undefined);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (theString.length == 0) {">
							<outline text="return (undefined);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="return (s);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertPost (item) { //convert a post received from WordPress to the struct defined by our API -- 9/12/23 by DW">
						<outline text="function getCatArray () {">
							<outline text="var catarray = new Array ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="for (var x in item.categories) {">
								<outline text="catarray.push (x);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (catarray);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function getCatstring () {">
							<outline text="var catstring = &quot;&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="for (var x in item.categories) {">
								<outline text="catstring += &quot;,&quot; + x;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (catstring.length &gt; 0) {">
								<outline text="catstring = utils.stringDelete (catstring, 1, 1);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (catstring);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function getMetadataObject (theArray) { //7/5/25 by DW">
							<outline text="var theObject = new Object ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="theArray.forEach (function (item) {">
								<outline text="theObject [item.key] = item.value;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (theObject);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function normalizeGuid (guid) { //3/13/26 by DW">
							<outline text="return guid.replace (/^https:\/\//i, 'http://');">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="idPost: item.ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idSite: item.site_ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="title: item.title,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="guid: normalizeGuid (item.guid), //3/13/26 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="content: item.content,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="type: item.type,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="categories: getCatArray (),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="metadata: getMetadataObject (item.metadata), //7/5/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="url: item.URL,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlShort: item.short_URL,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated: convertDate (item.date),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="author: {">
								<outline text="id: item.author.ID,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="username: item.author.login,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="name: item.author.name">
								</outline>
								<outline text="},">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertUser (theUser) {">
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="idUser: theUser.ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="name: theUser.display_name,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="username: theUser.username,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="email: theUser.email,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idPrimaryBlog: theUser.primary_blog,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlAvatar: theUser.avatar_URL, //3/17/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlPrimaryBlog: theUser.primary_blog_url,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlProfile: theUser.profile_URL, //3/17/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenStarted: convertDate (theUser.date),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="ctSites: theUser.site_count">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertSite (theSite) {">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/28/25; 8:52:00 AM by DW">
								<outline text="We don't get the options object if it's a site that's not on wordpress.com? So we don't know when the site was created. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const flDeleted = theSite.is_deleted; //1/24/25 by DW">
						</outline>
						<outline text="var whenCreated = undefined, ctPosts = undefined; //4/28/25 by DW">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (!flDeleted) {">
							<outline text="if (theSite.options !== undefined) { //4/28/25 by DW">
								<outline text="whenCreated = convertDate (theSite.options.created_at);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="ctPosts = theSite.options.post_count;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="idSite: theSite.ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlSite: theSite.URL,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="description: theSite.description,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="name: theSite.name,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated, //4/28/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated: (flDeleted) ? undefined : convertDate (theSite.options.created_at), //1/24/25 by DW" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="flDeleted, //1/24/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="ctPosts //4/28/25 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="ctPosts: theSite.options.post_count" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertSubscription (theSubscription) {">
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="id: theSubscription.ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idWpBlog: (theSubscription.blog_ID == &quot;0&quot;) ? undefined : theSubscription.blog_ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="feedUrl: theSubscription.URL, ">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenSubscribed: convertDate (theSubscription.date_subscribed)">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertMediaObject (theObject) {">
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="id: theObject.ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="url: theObject.URL,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated: theObject.date,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idPost: theObject.post_ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idAuthor: theObject.author_ID,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="type: theObject.mime_type,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="title: theObject.title,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="file: theObject.file, //11/13/24 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="guid: theObject.guid, //11/13/24 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="description: convertString (theObject.description),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="alt: convertString (theObject.alt),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="height: theObject.height,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="width: theObject.width">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertCategory (theCategory) { //10/20/24 by DW">
						<outline text="return ({">
							<outline text="id: theCategory.ID, //a number">
							</outline>
							<outline text="slug: theCategory.slug, //it's a unique identifier that's text, derived from the name of the category">
							</outline>
							<outline text="name: theCategory.name,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="description: theCategory.description,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="feedUrl: theCategory.feed_url,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idParent: (theCategory.parent == 0) ? undefined : theCategory.parent,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="ctPosts: theCategory.post_count">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getUserInfo (accessToken, callback) { //8/26/23 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="9/12/23; 1:16:00 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Return an abbreviated struct, not all the info that WordPress returns.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;getUserInfo: token == &quot; + accessToken); //3/12/25 by DW" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="wp.me ().get (function (err, theInfo) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertUser (theInfo));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getUserSites (accessToken, callback) { //8/26/23 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="9/12/23; 1:42:40 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Return an abbreviated struct for a site, not all the info that WordPress returns.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="wp.me ().sites (function (err, theSiteList) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theSiteList.sites.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="if (!item.is_deleted) { //1/24/25 by DW">
										<outline text="theList.push (convertSite (item));">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSitePosts (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //9/12/23 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="9/12/23; 11:44:15 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Return an abbreviated list of posts, not all the info that WordPress returns.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="site.postsList (function (err, thePosts) { //9/12/23 by DW">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="thePosts.posts.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="theList.push (convertPost (item));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="theList.push ({" isComment="true">
										<outline text="idPost: item.ID,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="idSite: item.site_ID,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="title: item.title,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="guid: item.guid,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="content: item.content,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="type: item.type,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="url: item.URL,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="urlShort: item.short_URL,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="whenCreated: new Date (item.date),">
										</outline>
										<outline text="author: {">
											<outline text="id: item.author.ID,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="username: item.author.login,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="name: item.author.name">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSiteUsers (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //8/28/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="site.usersList (function (err, theUsers) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theUsers.users.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="theList.push (convertUser (item));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSiteInfo (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //8/29/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="site.get (function (err, theInfo) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertSite (theInfo));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSiteMedialist (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //8/29/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="site.mediaList (function (err, theMedialist) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theMedialist.media.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="theList.push (convertMediaObject (item));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getPost (accessToken, idSite, idPost, callback) { //9/12/23 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="9/12/23; 12:34:36 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Return an abbreviated post, not all the info that WordPress returns.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const post = site.post (idPost);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="post.get (function (err, thePost) { //9/12/23 by DW">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertPost (thePost));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getPostAuthorInfo (idSite, idPost, callback) { //11/30/25 by DW">
						<outline text="getPost (undefined, idSite, idPost, function (err, thePost) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, thePost.author);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getObjectFromJsontext (jsontext, callback) {">
						<outline text="var theObject;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="try {">
							<outline text="theObject = JSON.parse (jsontext);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="catch (err) {">
							<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't add or update the post because the JSON text is not valid.&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="callback ({message});">
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (undefined);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (theObject);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getCategoriesObject (jstruct) {">
						<outline text="if (jstruct.categories === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return (undefined);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="var catstruct = new Object ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="jstruct.categories.forEach (function (item, ix) {">
								<outline text="catstruct [item] = {">
									<outline text="ID: ix + 1">
									</outline>
									<outline text="};">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (catstruct);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSiteCategories (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //10/19/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/24/25; 5:09:40 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Handle pagination. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="10/21/24; 11:32:17 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Don't return uncategorized. Our users are selecting from the other categories.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="10/19/24; 6:34:17 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Return the categories for a post. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const catsPerPage = 100; ">
						</outline>
						<outline text="var returnedCats = new Array ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="function nextPage (ixCat) {">
							<outline text="const options = {">
								<outline text="number: catsPerPage,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="offset: ixCat">
								</outline>
								<outline text="};">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="site.categoriesList (options, function (err, data) { ">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="data.categories.forEach (function (item) {">
										<outline text="if (item.slug != &quot;uncategorized&quot;) { //10/21/24 by DW">
											<outline text="returnedCats.push (convertCategory (item));">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="if (data.categories.length === catsPerPage) {">
										<outline text="nextPage (ixCat + catsPerPage);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="callback (undefined, returnedCats);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="nextPage (0);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSiteCategories (accessToken, idSite, callback) { //10/19/24 by DW" isComment="true">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="10/21/24; 11:32:17 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Don't return uncategorized. Our users are selecting from the other categories.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="10/19/24; 6:34:17 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Return the categories for a post. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="site.categoriesList (function (err, theCategories) { ">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var returnedCats = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theCategories.categories.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="if (item.slug != &quot;uncategorized&quot;) { //10/21/24 by DW">
										<outline text="returnedCats.push (convertCategory (item));">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, returnedCats);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function addSiteCategory (accessToken, idSite, jsontext, callback) { //3/15/25 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="3/15/25; 11:24:36 AM by DW">
								<outline text="This is what's in jsontext.">
									<outline text="{">
										<outline text="name: &quot;Tech News&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="slug: &quot;tech-news&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="description: &quot;Latest updates from the tech industry&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="parent: 0 // Use an existing category ID if needed">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const jstruct = getObjectFromJsontext (jsontext, callback);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (jstruct === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const theRequest = {">
							<outline text="method: &quot;POST&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="path: `/sites/${idSite}/categories/new`,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="body: jstruct">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="wp.req.post (theRequest, function (err, theCategory) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertCategory (theCategory));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deleteSiteCategory (accessToken, idSite, slug, callback) { //3/15/25 by DW">
						<outline text="const theRequest = {">
							<outline text="url: `https://public-api.wordpress.com/rest/v1.1/sites/${idSite}/categories/slug:${slug}/delete`,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="method: &quot;POST&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="headers: {">
								<outline text="'Authorization': `Bearer ${accessToken}`">
								</outline>
								<outline text="},">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="json: true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="request (theRequest, function (err, response, body) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="if ((response.statusCode &gt;= 200) &amp;&amp; (response.statusCode &lt;= 299)) {">
									<outline text="callback (undefined, body);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="const message = &quot;Couldn't read HTML page because status code == &quot; + response.statusCode;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback ({message});">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function updateSiteCategory (accessToken, idSite, slug, jsontext, callback) { //5/11/25 by DW">
						<outline text="const jstruct = getObjectFromJsontext (jsontext, callback);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (jstruct === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const theRequest = {">
							<outline text="method: &quot;POST&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="path: `/sites/${idSite}/categories/slug:${slug}`,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="path: `/sites/${idSite}/categories/${idCategory}`," isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="body: jstruct">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="wp.req.post (theRequest, function (err, theCategory) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertCategory (theCategory));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function uploadImage (accessToken, base64Data, filename, mimeType, idSite, callback) { //11/10/24 by DW">
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if ((idSite == undefined) || (idSite == &quot;undefined&quot;)) { //3/26/25 by DW">
							<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't upload the image because no site was specified.&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="callback ({message});">
							</outline>
							<outline text="return;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const imageBuffer = Buffer.from (base64Data, &quot;base64&quot;);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="function writeBufferToTempFile (callback) {">
							<outline text="const f = &quot;data/tmp/&quot; + idSite + &quot;/&quot; + filename;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="utils.sureFilePath (f, function () {">
								<outline text="fs.writeFile (f, imageBuffer, function (err) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="callback (undefined, f);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="writeBufferToTempFile (function (err, relpath) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const fileStream = fs.createReadStream (relpath);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="fileStream.on (&quot;close&quot;, function () {">
									<outline text="if (config.flDeleteTempFiles) {">
										<outline text="fs.unlink (relpath, function (err) {">
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="const theImage = {">
									<outline text="file: fileStream,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="filename,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="&quot;Content-Type&quot;: mimeType">
									</outline>
									<outline text="};">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="site.addMediaFiles (theImage, function (err, data) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (data.media.length == 0) {">
											<outline text="const message = &quot;No media files were uploaded.&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="callback (undefined, convertMediaObject (data.media [0]));">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function uploadImage (accessToken, imageBuffer, imageName, mimeType, idSite, callback) { //11/10/24 by DW" isComment="true">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="function writeBufferToTempFile (callback) {">
							<outline text="const f = &quot;data/tmp/1200.png&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="">
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;writeBufferToTempFile: imageBuffer.length == &quot; + imageBuffer.length);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;writeBufferToTempFile: Buffer.isBuffer (imageBuffer) == &quot; + Buffer.isBuffer (imageBuffer));">
							</outline>
							<outline text="">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (typeof imageBuffer === &quot;string&quot;) {">
								<outline text="imageBuffer = Buffer.from (imageBuffer, &quot;binary&quot;);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="">
							</outline>
							<outline text="utils.sureFilePath (f, function () {">
								<outline text="fs.writeFile (f, imageBuffer, function (err) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="callback (undefined, f);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="writeBufferToTempFile (function (err, relpath) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const fileStream = fs.createReadStream (relpath);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="fileStream.on (&quot;close&quot;, function () {">
									<outline text="fs.unlink (relpath, function (err) {">
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="const theImage = {">
									<outline text="file: fileStream,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="filename: imageName,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="'Content-Type': mimeType">
									</outline>
									<outline text="};">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="site.addMediaFiles (theImage, function (err, data) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="callback (undefined, convertMediaObject (data));">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="//storage">
					<outline text="var usernameCache = new Object ();">
					</outline>
					<outline text="var whenLastUsernameCacheStart = new Date ();">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSpecialDataFile (token, fname, callback) {">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const flprivate = true;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="readUserFile (username, fname, flprivate, 0, 0, function (err, theFile) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="console.log (&quot;getSpecialDataFile: fname == &quot; + fname + &quot;, theFile == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theFile));" isComment="true">
										</outline>
										<outline text="var flerror = false;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="try {">
											<outline text="theData = JSON.parse (theFile.filecontents);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="catch (err) {">
											<outline text="callback (err);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="flerror = true;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="if (!flerror) {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;getSpecialDataFile: fname == &quot; + fname + &quot;, theData == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theData));" isComment="true">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback (undefined, theData);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function emojiProcess (s) {">
						<outline text="function addSpan (code, name) {">
							<outline text="return (&quot;&lt;span class=\&quot;spEmoji\&quot;&gt;&quot; + code + &quot;&lt;/span&gt;&quot;);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (emoji.emojify (s, undefined, addSpan));">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function markdownProcess (s) {">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="11/16/24; 11:17:33 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Hold on we're supposed to be processing markdown text here. ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="Turning it back on. Geez.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="4/19/24; 11:30:21 AM by DW">
								<outline text="This is why Markdown can't work within something generated by MediumEditor. ">
									<outline text="MediumEditor generates a series of &lt;p&gt;.">
									</outline>
									<outline text="Markdown can't go into them, that's the rule of mixed markdown and html.">
									</outline>
									<outline text="So everything is within a &lt;p&gt; that means Markdown text will not be processed. ">
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="s = marked (s);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (s);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function processMarkdownImages (markdowntext) { //11/16/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="11/16/24; 10:18:43 AM by DW">
								<outline text="We convert markdown images to Gutenberg blocks describing an image.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (config.flConvertImagesToGutenberg) {">
							<outline text="const imageRegex = /!\[([^\]]*)\]\(([^)]+)\)/g;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="function processOneImage (alttext, url) {">
								<outline text="const templatetext = &quot;&lt;!-- wp:image {\&quot;id\&quot;:4375, \&quot;sizeSlug\&quot;: \&quot;large\&quot;} --&gt;\n&lt;figure class=\&quot;wp-block-image size-large is-resized\&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=\&quot;[%url%]\&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=\&quot;[%url%]\&quot; alt=\&quot;[%alttext%]\&quot; class=\&quot;wp-image-4375\&quot; style=\&quot;width:86px;height:auto\&quot;/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;\n&lt;!-- /wp:image --&gt;&quot;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const newtext = utils.multipleReplaceAll (templatetext, {alttext, url}, false, &quot;[%&quot;, &quot;%]&quot;);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="return (newtext);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="const newMarkdowntext = markdowntext.replace (imageRegex, function (match, altText, url) {">
								<outline text="return (processOneImage (altText, url));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (newMarkdowntext);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="return (markdowntext);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function processPostText (token, theText, theType, callback) {">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/13/26; 7:49:48 AM by DW">
								<outline text="new param, theType. only process text if contentType == markdown.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="only use the glossary if the feature is enabled.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (utils.stringLower (theType) == &quot;markdown&quot;) { //4/13/26 by DW">
							<outline text="theText = emojiProcess (theText); //4/15/24 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="theText = processMarkdownImages (theText); //11/16/24 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="theText = markdownProcess (theText); //4/18/24 by DW">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (config.flUseGlossary) { //4/13/26 by DW">
								<outline text="getSpecialDataFile (token, &quot;glossary.json&quot;, function (err, theGlossary) {">
									<outline text="if (!err) {">
										<outline text="theText = utils.multipleReplaceAll (theText, theGlossary, false);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theText);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theText);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="callback (undefined, theText); //return text unprocessed">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function logPublish (verb, theData) { //2/23/25 by DW">
						<outline text="const eventData = {">
							<outline text="title: theData.title,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="author: theData.author.username,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="url: theData.url,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenCreated: theData.whenCreated" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="addToLog (verb + &quot;Post&quot;, undefined, eventData);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getMetadataForPost (theDraft) { //7/5/25 by DW -- xxx">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="7/5/25; 10:32:56 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Create a metadata object suitable for including in the post structure to be sent to wordpress.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="It looks something like this">
									<outline text="metadata: [">
										<outline text="{">
											<outline text="key: &quot;source_app&quot;,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="value: &quot;wpidentity&quot;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="},">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="{">
											<outline text="key: &quot;post_type&quot;,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="value: &quot;generated&quot;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="]">
										</outline>
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="var theMetadata = {">
							<outline text="apiVersion: &quot;0.4.0&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="title: theDraft.title,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="linksTo: &quot;&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="markdowntext: &quot;&quot;,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="idDraft: theDraft.idDraft,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (theDraft.linkblogLink !== undefined) {">
							<outline text="theMetadata.linksTo = theDraft.linkblogLink;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (theDraft.contentType == &quot;markdown&quot;) {">
							<outline text="theMetadata.markdowntext = theDraft.content;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="var theArray = new Array ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="for (var key in theMetadata) {">
							<outline text="theArray.push ({">
								<outline text="key: config.postMetadataPrefix + &quot;_&quot; + key, //wordlandTitle for example">
								</outline>
								<outline text="value: theMetadata [key]">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;getMetadataForPost: theArray == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theArray));">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (theArray);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getWordlandPrefs (username, callback) { //12/1/25 by DW">
						<outline text="const fname = &quot;wordland/prefs.json&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const flprivate = true;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="readUserFile (username, fname, flprivate, 0, 0, function (err, theFile) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var flerror = false;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="try {">
									<outline text="theData = JSON.parse (theFile.filecontents);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="catch (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="flerror = true;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (!flerror) {">
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theData);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function processReply (inReplyTo, theDraft) { //12/1/25 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="12/3/25; 11:29:07 AM by DW">
								<outline text="The draft might be a reply. If we can find an email address for the author of inReplyTo, we send notification, and add an edge record for the connection.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function sendNotification (email, inReplyTo, theDraft) {">
							<outline text="const mailtext = `">
								<outline text="&lt;div&gt;">
									<outline text="&lt;blockquote&gt;">
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;idSite: ${theDraft.idSite}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;idPost: ${theDraft.idPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;url: ${theDraft.url}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;content: ${theDraft.content}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;title: ${theDraft.title}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.id: ${theDraft.author.id}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.name: ${theDraft.author.name}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.username: ${theDraft.author.username}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.idSite: ${inReplyTo.idSite}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.idPost: ${inReplyTo.idPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.urlPost: ${inReplyTo.urlPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;/blockquote&gt;">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="&lt;/div&gt;">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="`;">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="const title = &quot;wpIdentity: &quot; + nowstring ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="const mailsender = &quot;dave@scripting.com&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: mailtext == &quot; + mailtext);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="mail.send (email, title, mailtext, mailsender, function (err, data) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: data == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (data));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (inReplyTo !== undefined) {">
							<outline text="getPostAuthorInfo (inReplyTo.idSite, inReplyTo.idPost, function (err, theAuthor) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: theAuthor == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theAuthor));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="getWordlandPrefs (theAuthor.username, function (err, thePrefs) {">
										<outline text="if (err) {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: thePrefs == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (thePrefs));">
											</outline>
											<outline text="if (utils.getBoolean (thePrefs.flNotifyForReplies)) {">
												<outline text="const email = utils.trimWhitespace (thePrefs.emailForNotification);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="if (email.length &gt; 0) {">
													<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: email == &quot; + email);">
													</outline>
													<outline text="sendNotification (email, inReplyTo, theDraft);">
													</outline>
													<outline text="">
													</outline>
													<outline text="const idSourceSite = theDraft.idSite, idSourcePost = theDraft.idPost;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="const idDestSite = inReplyTo.idSite, idDestPost = inReplyTo.idPost;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="const sourceAuthor = theDraft.author.username, destAuthor = theAuthor.username;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="">
													</outline>
													<outline text="addEdge (idSourceSite, idSourcePost, sourceAuthor, idDestSite, idDestPost, destAuthor, function (err, insertId) {">
														<outline text="if (err) {">
															<outline text="console.log (&quot;addEdge: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
															</outline>
															<outline text="}">
															</outline>
														</outline>
														<outline text="else {">
															<outline text="console.log (&quot;addEdge: insertId == &quot; + insertId);">
															</outline>
															<outline text="}">
															</outline>
														</outline>
														<outline text="});">
														</outline>
													</outline>
													<outline text="}">
													</outline>
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function processReply (theDraft) { //12/1/25 by DW" isComment="true">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="12/3/25; 11:29:07 AM by DW">
								<outline text="The draft is a reply. If we can find an email address for the author of the original post, we send notification, and add an edge record for the connection.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function sendNotification (email, theDraft) {">
							<outline text="const inReplyTo = theDraft.inReplyTo;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="const mailtext = `">
								<outline text="&lt;div&gt;">
									<outline text="&lt;blockquote&gt;">
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;idSite: ${theDraft.idSite}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;idPost: ${theDraft.idPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;url: ${theDraft.url}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;content: ${theDraft.content}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;title: ${theDraft.title}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.id: ${theDraft.author.id}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.name: ${theDraft.author.name}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;author.username: ${theDraft.author.username}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.idSite: ${inReplyTo.idSite}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.idPost: ${inReplyTo.idPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;p&gt;inReplyTo.urlPost: ${inReplyTo.urlPost}&lt;/p&gt;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&lt;/blockquote&gt;">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="&lt;/div&gt;">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="`;">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="const title = &quot;wpIdentity: &quot; + nowstring ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="const mailsender = &quot;dave@scripting.com&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: mailtext == &quot; + mailtext);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="mail.send (email, title, mailtext, mailsender, function (err, data) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;sendNotification: data == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (data));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (theDraft.inReplyTo !== undefined) {">
							<outline text="const inReplyTo = theDraft.inReplyTo;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="getPostAuthorInfo (inReplyTo.idSite, inReplyTo.idPost, function (err, theAuthor) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: theAuthor == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theAuthor));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="getWordlandPrefs (theAuthor.username, function (err, thePrefs) {">
										<outline text="if (err) {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: thePrefs == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (thePrefs));">
											</outline>
											<outline text="if (utils.getBoolean (thePrefs.flNotifyForReplies)) {">
												<outline text="const email = utils.trimWhitespace (thePrefs.emailForNotification);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="if (email.length &gt; 0) {">
													<outline text="console.log (&quot;testNotification: email == &quot; + email);">
													</outline>
													<outline text="sendNotification (email, theDraft);">
													</outline>
													<outline text="">
													</outline>
													<outline text="const idSourceSite = theDraft.idSite, idSourcePost = theDraft.idPost;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="const idDestSite = inReplyTo.idSite, idDestPost = inReplyTo.idPost;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="addEdge (idSourceSite, idSourcePost, idDestSite, idDestPost, function (err, insertId) {">
														<outline text="if (err) {">
															<outline text="console.log (&quot;addEdge: err.message == &quot; + err.message);">
															</outline>
															<outline text="}">
															</outline>
														</outline>
														<outline text="else {">
															<outline text="console.log (&quot;addEdge: insertId == &quot; + insertId);">
															</outline>
															<outline text="}">
															</outline>
														</outline>
														<outline text="});">
														</outline>
													</outline>
													<outline text="}">
													</outline>
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function addPost (accessToken, idSite, jsontext, callback) { //8/29/23 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="2/9/26; 4:36:26 PM by DW">
								<outline text="If the jsontext obj has an inReplyTo object, we copy it into the draft we return.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="5/13/24; 10:20:55 AM by DW">
								<outline text="We weren't calling processPostText. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="9/13/23; 11:13:55 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Convert the external format to the one required by the WordPress api. ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="We hard-code a lot of options that maybe we'll want to allow the caller to specify later, but for now I don't know what the call those options, so we'll come back to this.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="8/29/23; 12:44:12 PM by DW">
								<outline text="thePost should contain values like title, content, status, date, categories...">
								</outline>
								<outline text="I got a good list from ChatGPT but haven't yet found the place where they're defined by WordPress.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const jstruct = getObjectFromJsontext (jsontext, callback);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (jstruct === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="testNotification (jstruct); //12/1/25 by DW -- testing" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="processPostText (accessToken, jstruct.content, jstruct.contentType, function (err, theProcessedContent) { //5/13/24 by DW">
							<outline text="const thePost = {">
								<outline text="title: jstruct.title,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="content: theProcessedContent, //5/13/24 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="categories: jstruct.categories, //10/21/24 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="categories: getCategoriesObject (jstruct), //9/14/23 by DW" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="excerpt: jstruct.excerpt, //3/22/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="featured_image: jstruct.idFeaturedImage, //3/22/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="status: &quot;publish&quot;,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="date: new Date ().toGMTString (),">
								</outline>
								<outline text="format: &quot;standard&quot;,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="comment_status: &quot;open&quot;,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="metadata: getMetadataForPost (jstruct) //7/5/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="};">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;addPost: thePost == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (thePost)); //5/8/24 by DW" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="site.addPost (thePost, function (err, theNewPost) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;addPost: err.message == &quot; + err.message); //5/8/24 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="var theConvertedPost = convertPost (theNewPost); //5/17/24 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="theConvertedPost.whenPublished = new Date ();">
									</outline>
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;addPost: theConvertedPost == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theConvertedPost)); //5/8/24 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="logPublish (&quot;add&quot;, theConvertedPost); //2/23/25 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="processReply (jstruct.inReplyTo, theConvertedPost); //12/3/25 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="if (jstruct.inReplyTo !== undefined) { //2/9/26 by DW">
										<outline text="theConvertedPost.inReplyTo = jstruct.inReplyTo;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theConvertedPost);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function updatePost (accessToken, idSite, idPost, jsontext, callback) { //8/29/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const jstruct = getObjectFromJsontext (jsontext, callback);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (jstruct === undefined) {">
							<outline text="return;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="testNotification (jstruct); //12/1/25 by DW -- testing" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const post = site.post (idPost);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="processPostText (accessToken, jstruct.content, jstruct.contentType, function (err, theProcessedContent) {">
							<outline text="const thePost = {">
								<outline text="title: jstruct.title,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="content: theProcessedContent,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="categories: jstruct.categories, //10/21/24 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="categories: getCategoriesObject (jstruct), //9/14/23 by DW" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="excerpt: jstruct.excerpt, //3/22/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="featured_image: jstruct.idFeaturedImage, //3/22/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="status: &quot;publish&quot;,">
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="metadata: getMetadataForPost (jstruct) //7/5/25 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="};">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="post.update (thePost, function (err, theNewPost) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="var theConvertedPost = convertPost (theNewPost); //5/17/24 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="theConvertedPost.whenPublished = new Date ();">
									</outline>
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;updatePost: theConvertedPost == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (theConvertedPost)); //5/8/24 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="logPublish (&quot;update&quot;, theConvertedPost); //2/23/25 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="processReply (jstruct.inReplyTo, theConvertedPost); //12/3/25 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theConvertedPost);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deletePost (accessToken, idSite, idPost, callback) { //9/4/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const site = wp.site (idSite);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="const post = site.post (idPost);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="post.delete (function (err, theDeletedPost) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, convertPost (theDeletedPost));">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSubscriptions (accessToken, callback) { //9/5/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const wp = wpcom (accessToken);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="wp.req.get (&quot;/read/following/mine&quot;, {}, function (err, theSubscriptionList) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theSubscriptionList.subscriptions.forEach (function (item) {">
									<outline text="theList.push (convertSubscription (item));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function startStorage (theDatabase, callback) { //3/24/24 by DW">
						<outline text="function getMysqlVersion (callback) {">
							<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select version () as version;&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
								<outline text="var theVersion = undefined;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (!err) {">
									<outline text="if (result.length &gt; 0) {">
										<outline text="theVersion = result [0].version;">
										</outline>
										<outline text="console.log (&quot;getMysqlVersion: theVersion == &quot; + theVersion);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theVersion);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.start (config.database, function () {">
							<outline text="getMysqlVersion (function (err, mysqlVersion) { //11/18/23 by DW, 2/1/24; 11:22:16 AM by DW">
								<outline text="config.flStorageEnabled = true;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="config.mysqlVersion = mysqlVersion;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (callback !== undefined) {">
									<outline text="callback (undefined, config);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function convertStorageItem (item) { //5/16/24 by DW -- convert database item to the item struct defined by the API">
						<outline text="if (item.idSite == 0) {">
							<outline text="item.idSite = undefined;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (item.idPost == 0) {">
							<outline text="item.idPost = undefined;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (item);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function readUserFile (username, relpath, flprivate, idsite, idpost, callback) {">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="2/22/25; 9:27:30 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Send back a value in the error object that indicates clearly that the error was that the file doesn't exist. ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="I don't want to be looking for a string, because that would break if the error message ever changed. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const privateval = (flprivate) ? 1 : 0;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="var sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + &quot; and flprivate = &quot; + davesql.encode (privateval)">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (idsite !== undefined) { //4/5/24 by DW">
							<outline text="sqltext += &quot; and idsite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idsite);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (idpost !== undefined) {">
							<outline text="sqltext += &quot; and idpost = &quot; + davesql.encode (idpost);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="sqltext += &quot;;&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;readUserFile: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext); //4/14/24 by DW" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;readUserFile: username == &quot; + username + &quot;, relpath == &quot; + relpath); //9/21/23 by DW" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
									<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't find the file &quot; + relpath + &quot; for the user &quot; + username + &quot;.&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="const code = 404; //2/22/25 by DW">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback ({message, code});">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="const theFileRec = result [0];">
									</outline>
									<outline text="const theReturnedData = {" isComment="true">
										<outline text="filedata: theFileRec.filecontents.toString (),">
										</outline>
										<outline text="filestats: {">
											<outline text="relpath: theFileRec.relpath,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="type: theFileRec.type,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="username: theFileRec.username,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="flprivate: theFileRec.flprivate,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="ctSaves: theFileRec.ctSaves,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="whenCreated: theFileRec.whenCreated,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="whenUpdated: theFileRec.whenUpdated">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="};">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theFileRec);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function readWholeFile (token, relpath, flprivate, idsite, idpost, callback) { //3/24/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/5/24; 12:31:36 PM by DW">
								<outline text="New optional params, idsite and idpost.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="3/29/24; 9:29:20 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Just returning the content of the record from the database, no funny structures.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="readUserFile (username, relpath, flprivate, idsite, idpost, callback);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function writeWholeFile (token, relpath, type, flprivate, filecontents, idsite, idpost, iddraft, callback) { ">
						<outline text="const now = new Date ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="function getEncodedValues (jstruct) {">
									<outline text="var values = davesql.encodeValues (jstruct);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="values = utils.stringMid (values, 1, values.length - 1); //remove extraneous semicolon at the end">
									</outline>
									<outline text="return (values);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="function getValuesForUpdating (theValues) { //this could go into the davesql package">
									<outline text="var s = &quot;&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="for (var x in theValues) {">
										<outline text="if (s.length &gt; 0) {">
											<outline text="s += &quot;, &quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="s += x + &quot;=&quot; + davesql.encode (theValues [x]);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="return (s);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="function setUrlpublic () { //5/16/24 by DW">
									<outline text="if (!flprivate) { //5/16/24 by DW">
										<outline text="if (idsite !== undefined) {">
											<outline text="fileRec.urlPublic = config.urlPublicUserFiles + username + &quot;/&quot; + idsite + &quot;/&quot; + relpath">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="function logWrite (verb) { //12/21/24 by DW">
									<outline text="const eventData = {">
										<outline text="username, relpath, iddraft">
										</outline>
										<outline text="};">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="addToLog (verb + &quot;File&quot;, undefined, eventData);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="const privateval = (flprivate) ? 1 : 0;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="var fileRec = {">
									<outline text="username, ">
									</outline>
									<outline text="relpath, ">
									</outline>
									<outline text="type,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="flprivate: privateval,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="filecontents,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="whenUpdated: now">
									</outline>
									<outline text="};">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (idsite !== undefined) {">
									<outline text="fileRec.idSite = idsite;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (idpost !== undefined) {">
									<outline text="fileRec.idPost = idpost;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (iddraft !== undefined) { //5/11/24 by DW">
									<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;update wpstorage set &quot; + getValuesForUpdating (fileRec) + &quot;, ctSaves = ctSaves + 1 where id = &quot; + davesql.encode (iddraft) + &quot;;&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
										<outline text="if (err) {">
											<outline text="callback (err);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="if (result.affectedRows == 0) {">
												<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't update the file because there is no record with id == &quot; + iddraft;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="callback ({message});">
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="else {">
												<outline text="fileRec.id = iddraft;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="setUrlpublic (); //5/16/24 by DW">
												</outline>
												<outline text="logWrite (&quot;update&quot;); //12/21/24 by DW">
												</outline>
												<outline text="callback (undefined, fileRec);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="fileRec.whenCreated = now;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="fileRec.ctSaves = 1;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="const onDuplicatePart = &quot;on duplicate key update type = values (type), filecontents = values (filecontents), whenUpdated = &quot; + davesql.encode (now) + &quot;, ctSaves = ctSaves + 1&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;insert into wpstorage &quot; + getEncodedValues (fileRec) + &quot; &quot; + onDuplicatePart + &quot;;&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
										<outline text="if (err) {">
											<outline text="callback (err);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="fileRec.id = result.insertId;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="setUrlpublic (); //5/16/24 by DW">
											</outline>
											<outline text="logWrite (&quot;create&quot;); //12/21/24 by DW">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback (undefined, fileRec);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function writeUniqueFile (token, relpath, type, flprivate, filecontents, idsite, idpost, callback) { //5/12/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="5/12/24; 8:46:30 AM by DW">
								<outline text="writeWholeFile is the general-purpose routine, this is for files that can only have one instance per path/type/etc">
								</outline>
								<outline text="examples include the user's prefs.json file for a specific app, or the user's glossary.json file. ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="these files are a lot simpler to work with than the draft.json files.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="we could manage these files ourselves at a higher level, but that would mean we would have to remember the id of the glossary.json file, in order to save it.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="it's simpler to just provide a new entrypoint for these files that finds the id before writing it, the info is after all, in the database. ;-)">
								</outline>
								<outline text="this could be done on the client, but that means two round trips for the data. this is a little more efficient. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="readWholeFile (token, relpath, flprivate, idsite, idpost, function (err, theOriginalFile) {">
							<outline text="const id = (err) ? undefined : theOriginalFile.id; //if id is undefined, treat it as a new file">
							</outline>
							<outline text="writeWholeFile (token, relpath, type, flprivate, filecontents, idsite, idpost, id, callback);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deleteFile (token, relpath, flprivate, callback) { //3/26/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="5/10/24; 12:19:38 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Shouldn't this function take an idsite and idpost params?">
								</outline>
								<outline text="Or possibly an id??">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const now = new Date ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const privateval = (flprivate) ? 1 : 0;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;delete from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + &quot; and flprivate = &quot; + davesql.encode (privateval) + &quot;;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
											<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't find the file &quot; + relpath + &quot; for the user &quot; + username + &quot;.&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="callback (undefined, true);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getRecentUserDrafts (token, maxCtDraftsParam, idSiteParam, callback) { //4/27/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="10/26/24; 8:50:09 AM by DW">
								<outline text="We were getting the most recent drafts for all users, but we must restrict it to the user. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="5/8/24; 5:21:12 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Changed the ordering to order by whenUpdated. There's only one draft that hasn't been saved, at least right now. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="4/30/24; 10:04:43 AM by DW">
								<outline text="New optional param, idSiteParam. If provided we only return drafts from a single site. Useful for building feeds. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="4/27/24; 9:26:03 AM by DW">
								<outline text="get draft.json files for a specific user in reverse chronologic order">
									<outline text="select username, relpath, flprivate, idsite, idpost, type, whenCreated, whenUpdated, ctsaves from wpstorage where relpath = 'draft.json' order by whenCreated desc limit 10;" isComment="true">
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const now = new Date ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="var sitepart = &quot;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (idSiteParam !== undefined) {">
									<outline text="sitepart = &quot; and idsite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idSiteParam) + &quot; &quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="const maxCtDrafts = Math.min (config.maxCtDrafts, maxCtDraftsParam);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where relpath = 'draft.json' and username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) +  sitepart + &quot; order by whenUpdated desc limit &quot; + maxCtDrafts + &quot;;&quot;; //10/26/24 by DW">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where relpath = 'draft.json' &quot; +  sitepart + &quot;order by whenUpdated desc limit &quot; + maxCtDrafts + &quot;;&quot;;" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where relpath = 'draft.json' &quot; +  sitepart + &quot;order by whenCreated desc limit &quot; + maxCtDrafts + &quot;;&quot;;" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;\ngetRecentUserDrafts: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext + &quot;\n&quot;);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="var theArray = new Array ();">
										</outline>
										<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
											<outline text="const jstruct = JSON.parse (item.filecontents);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.idDraft = item.id; //copy data from database for use in the app -- 5/12/24 by DW">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.whenCreated = new Date (item.whenCreated);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.whenUpdated = new Date (item.whenUpdated); ">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.ctSaves = item.ctSaves; ">
											</outline>
											<outline text="">
											</outline>
											<outline text="theArray.push (jstruct);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="callback (undefined, theArray);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getUserFileInfo (token, maxFiles, callback) { //5/16/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="5/16/24; 11:36:21 AM by DW">
								<outline text="For debugging at least to start.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) { ">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const maxCtFiles = Math.min (config.maxCtFiles, maxFiles);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; order by id asc limit &quot; + maxCtFiles + &quot;;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;getUserFileInfo: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="var theArray = new Array ();">
										</outline>
										<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
											<outline text="theArray.push (convertStorageItem (item));">
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="callback (undefined, theArray);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function readDraft (token, iddraft, callback) { //5/29/24 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="10/17/24; 12:30:16 PM by DW">
								<outline text="it would crash if there was no record with id == iddraft. we were checking the wrong value. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="5/29/24; 9:41:41 AM by DW">
								<outline text="Special way to read a file based on the id, useful for bookmarks in wordland. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and id = &quot; + davesql.encode (iddraft) + &quot;;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;readDraft: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (result.length == 0) { //10/17/24 by DW">
											<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the file because there is no record with id == &quot; + iddraft;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="callback (undefined, result [0]);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deleteDraft (token, iddraft, callback) { //5/29/24 by DW">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;delete from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and id = &quot; + davesql.encode (iddraft) + &quot;;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;deleteDraft: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="callback (undefined, true);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getNextDraft (token, id, flPrev, callback) { //10/29/24 by DW">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const chCompare = (flPrev) ? &quot; &lt; &quot; : &quot; &gt; &quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const ascendOrDescend = (flPrev) ? &quot; desc &quot; : &quot; asc &quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select *  from wpstorage  where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (&quot;draft.json&quot;) + &quot; and id &quot; + chCompare + davesql.encode (id) + &quot; order by id &quot; + ascendOrDescend + &quot; limit 1;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;getNextDraft: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
											<outline text="const which = (flPrev) ? &quot;previous&quot; : &quot;next&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the next draft because there is no &quot; + which + &quot; draft.&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="const jsontext = result [0].filecontents;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="const draftInfo = JSON.parse (jsontext);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback (undefined, draftInfo);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getNextPrevArray (token, callback) { //11/1/24 by DW">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const relpath = &quot;draft.json&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select id  from wpstorage  where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + &quot; order by id  asc;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;getNextPrevArray: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
											<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the next/prevs because the user \&quot;&quot; + username + &quot;\&quot; has no drafts.&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="const theArray = new Array ();">
											</outline>
											<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
												<outline text="theArray.push (item.id);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="});">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback (undefined, theArray);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function isUserWhitelisted (token, callback) { //10/24/24 by DW">
						<outline text="if (config.flUseWhitelist) {">
							<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="var flWhitelisted = false;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="config.authorizedAccounts.forEach (function (item) {">
										<outline text="if (item == username) {">
											<outline text="flWhitelisted = true;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, flWhitelisted);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="callback (undefined, true); //if not using whitelist, everyone is whitelisted">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function isUserSysop (username, callback) { ">
						<outline text="if (config.sysopUsername === undefined) { //2/24/25 by DW">
							<outline text="return (true); //everyone is authorized">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (username == config.sysopUsername) {">
							<outline text="return (true); ">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get this information because you are not authorized.&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="callback ({message});">
							</outline>
							<outline text="return (false);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getTopUsers (username, callback) { //12/23/24 by DW">
						<outline text="if (isUserSysop (username, callback)) {">
							<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select id, username, whenCreated, whenUpdated, ctSaves from wpstorage where relpath = 'wordland/prefs.json' order by ctSaves desc limit 100;&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
									</outline>
									<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
										<outline text="theList.push ({">
											<outline text="username: item.username,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="ctConnects: item.ctSaves,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="whenFirstConnect: item.whenCreated,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="whenLastConnect: item.whenUpdated">
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getNewPosts (username, callback) { //2/24/25 by DW">
						<outline text="if (isUserSysop (username, callback)) {">
							<outline text="const sqltext = `">
								<outline text="select l.*">
								</outline>
								<outline text="from log l">
								</outline>
								<outline text="join (">
									<outline text="select json_extract(eventData, '$.url') as postUrl, max(whenCreated) as latestWhenCreated">
									</outline>
									<outline text="from log">
									</outline>
									<outline text="where eventName in ('addPost', 'updatePost')">
									</outline>
									<outline text="group by json_extract(eventData, '$.url')">
									</outline>
									<outline text="order by latestWhenCreated desc">
									</outline>
									<outline text="limit 100">
									</outline>
									<outline text=") latest">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="on json_extract(l.eventData, '$.url') = latest.postUrl">
								</outline>
								<outline text="and l.whenCreated = latest.latestWhenCreated">
								</outline>
								<outline text="order by l.whenCreated desc">
								</outline>
								<outline text="limit 100;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="select l.*" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="from log l" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="join (" isComment="true">
									<outline text="select json_extract(eventData, '$.url') as postUrl, max(whenCreated) as latestWhenCreated">
									</outline>
									<outline text="from log">
									</outline>
									<outline text="where eventName in ('addPost', 'updatePost')">
									</outline>
									<outline text="group by json_extract(eventData, '$.url')">
									</outline>
									<outline text=") latest">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="on json_extract(l.eventData, '$.url') = latest.postUrl" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="and l.whenCreated = latest.latestWhenCreated;" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="`;">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
								<outline text="if (err) {">
									<outline text="callback (err);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="var theList = new Array ();">
									</outline>
									<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
										<outline text="{" isComment="true">
											<outline text="&quot;id&quot;: 11101,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="&quot;eventName&quot;: &quot;updatePost&quot;,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="&quot;eventError&quot;: &quot;&quot;,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="&quot;eventData&quot;: &quot;{\&quot;url\&quot;: \&quot;https://daveverse.wordpress.com/2025/02/24/757/\&quot;, \&quot;title\&quot;: \&quot;Mission accomplished\&quot;, \&quot;author\&quot;: \&quot;scripting\&quot;}&quot;,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="&quot;whenCreated&quot;: &quot;2025-02-24T14:38:21.000Z&quot;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}," isComment="true">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="const jstruct = JSON.parse (item.eventData);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="theList.push ({">
											<outline text="id: item.id,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="title: (jstruct.title === undefined) ? &quot;&quot; : jstruct.title,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="url: jstruct.url,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="author: jstruct.author,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="when: item.whenCreated,">
											</outline>
											<outline text="event: item.eventName">
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, theList);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getPublicFile (username, relpath, callback) { //1/9/25 by DW">
						<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from  wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + &quot; and flprivate = 0;&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
									<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't find the file &quot; + relpath + &quot; for the user &quot; + username + &quot;, or it may not be public.&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback ({message});">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="const theFile = result [0];">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback (undefined, JSON.parse (theFile.filecontents));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getAllDraftsForUser (token, callback) { //3/19/25 by DW">
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const relpath = &quot;draft.json&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select *  from wpstorage  where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + &quot; order by id  asc;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
											<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the next/prevs because the user \&quot;&quot; + username + &quot;\&quot; has no drafts.&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback ({message});">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="const theArray = new Array ();">
											</outline>
											<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
												<outline text="const jstruct = JSON.parse (item.filecontents)">
												</outline>
												<outline text="jstruct.idDraft = item.id;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="jstruct.ctSaves = item.ctSaves; ">
												</outline>
												<outline text="theArray.push (jstruct);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="});">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="callback (undefined, theArray);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getRangeOfDraftsForUser (token, idLowest, ct, callback) { //8/5/25 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="8/5/25; 10:27:20 AM by DW">
								<outline text="If idLowest is undefined, get the first ct drafts, otherwise it should be lowest id in the last batch, and we'll get the next ct drafts after that id.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="If we're out of drafts return an empty array.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="getUsername (token, function (err, username) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="} ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const relpath = &quot;draft.json&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const extrabit = (idLowest === undefined) ? &quot;&quot; : ` and id &lt; ${davesql.encode (idLowest)} `;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select *  from wpstorage  where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath = &quot; + davesql.encode (relpath) + extrabit + &quot; order by id  desc limit &quot; + ct + &quot;;&quot;;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;getRangeOfDraftsForUser: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);" isComment="true">
								</outline>
								<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
									<outline text="if (err) {">
										<outline text="callback (err);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="else {">
										<outline text="const theArray = new Array ();">
										</outline>
										<outline text="result.forEach (function (item) {">
											<outline text="const jstruct = JSON.parse (item.filecontents);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.idDraft = item.id;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="jstruct.ctSaves = item.ctSaves; ">
											</outline>
											<outline text="theArray.push (jstruct);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="callback (undefined, theArray);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getDraftFromUrl (url, callback) { //8/17/25 by DW" isComment="true">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="8/17/25; 12:21:41 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Created. But I'm not sure we need this. ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const sqltext = `">
							<outline text="select json_extract(filecontents, '$.idDraft') as idDraft from wpstorage">
							</outline>
							<outline text="where json_unquote(json_extract(filecontents, '$.url')) = ${davesql.encode (url)};">
							</outline>
							<outline text="`;">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;getDraftFromUrl: sqltext == &quot; + sqltext);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
									<outline text="const message = &quot;Can't get the file because there is no record with url == &quot; + url;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback ({message});">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="callback (undefined, result [0]);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getWordlandDraft (idSite, idPost, callback) { //3/16/26 by DW">
						<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where idSite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idSite) + &quot; and idPost = &quot; + davesql.encode (idPost) + &quot; and relpath = 'draft.json' limit 1;&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="if (result.length == 0) {">
									<outline text="const message = &quot;No draft found for this post.&quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="callback ({message});">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="else {">
									<outline text="callback (undefined, convertStorageItem (result [0]));">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getSourceFiles (username, idsite, idpost, callback) { //4/11/26 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/11/26; 12:46:06 PM by DW">
								<outline text="get names of files whose names are like source.opml or source.gutenberg.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="const sqltext = &quot;select * from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath like 'source.%' and idsite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idsite) + &quot; and idpost = &quot; + davesql.encode (idpost) + &quot;;&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="const theFiles = result.map (function (row) {">
									<outline text="return ({">
										<outline text="relpath: row.relpath,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="filecontents: row.filecontents,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="type: row.type,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="whenCreated: row.whenCreated,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="whenUpdated: row.whenUpdated">
										</outline>
										<outline text="});">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="callback (undefined, theFiles);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deleteSourceFiles (username, idsite, idpost, pathsToDelete, callback) { //4/11/26 by DW">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="4/11/26; 6:46:29 PM by DW">
								<outline text="if pathsToDelete, an array, is undefined, delete all source.* files for the indicated idsite, idpost. if it is specified, only delete the named files.  ">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="var sqltext = &quot;delete from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and idsite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idsite) + &quot; and idpost = &quot; + davesql.encode (idpost);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="if ((pathsToDelete !== undefined) &amp;&amp; (pathsToDelete.length &gt; 0)) {">
							<outline text="var encodedNames = &quot;&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="pathsToDelete.forEach (function (item) {">
								<outline text="if (encodedNames.length &gt; 0) {">
									<outline text="encodedNames += &quot;, &quot;;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="encodedNames += davesql.encode (item);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="sqltext += &quot; and relpath in (&quot; + encodedNames + &quot;);&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="sqltext += &quot; and relpath like 'source.%';&quot;;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, result.affectedRows);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function deleteSourceFiles (username, idsite, idpost, callback) { //4/11/26 by DW" isComment="true">
						<outline text="var sqltext = &quot;delete from wpstorage where username = &quot; + davesql.encode (username) + &quot; and relpath like 'source.%' and idsite = &quot; + davesql.encode (idsite) + &quot; and idpost = &quot; + davesql.encode (idpost) + &quot;;&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="davesql.runSqltext (sqltext, function (err, result) {">
							<outline text="if (err) {">
								<outline text="callback (err);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="callback (undefined, result.affectedRows);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
				</outline>
				<outline text="//sockets -- 5/24/24 by DW">
					<outline text="var theWsServer = undefined;">
					</outline>
					<outline text="">
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getWsProtocol () { //2/8/23 by DW">
						<outline text="const protocol = (utils.getBoolean (config.flSecureWebsocket)) ? &quot;wss://&quot; : &quot;ws://&quot;;">
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (protocol);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function notifySocketSubscribers (verb, payload, flPayloadIsString, callbackToQualify) {">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="3/6/21; 12:36:58 PM by DW">
								<outline text="New optional param, flPayloadIsString. If true we don't treat the payload as if it were a JS object. ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="New optional param, callbackToQualify, if specified we call it on each connection, if it returns true it qualifies to be notified">
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="if (theWsServer !== undefined) {">
							<outline text="var ctUpdates = 0, now = new Date (), ctTotalSockets = 0;">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (payload !== undefined) { ">
								<outline text="if (!flPayloadIsString) {">
									<outline text="payload = utils.jsonStringify (payload);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="theWsServer.clients.forEach (function (conn, ix) {">
								<outline text="ctTotalSockets++;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (conn.appData !== undefined) { //it's one of ours">
									<outline text="var flnotify = true;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="if (callbackToQualify !== undefined) {">
										<outline text="flnotify = callbackToQualify (conn);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="if (flnotify) {">
										<outline text="try {">
											<outline text="conn.sendText (verb + &quot;\r&quot; + payload);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="conn.appData.whenLastUpdate = now;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="conn.appData.ctUpdates++;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="ctUpdates++;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="catch (err) {">
											<outline text="console.log (&quot;notifySocketSubscribers: socket #&quot; + i + &quot;: error updating&quot;);">
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;\nnotifySocketSubscribers: &quot; + ctUpdates + &quot; of &quot; + ctTotalSockets + &quot; sockets were updated.\n&quot;);" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function checkWebSocketCalls () { //expire timed-out calls">
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function countOpenSockets () {">
						<outline text="if (theWsServer === undefined) { //12/18/15 by DW">
							<outline text="return (0);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="else {">
							<outline text="return (theWsServer.clients.length);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function getOpenSocketsArray () { //return an array with data about open sockets">
						<outline text="var theArray = new Array ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="theWsServer.clients.forEach (function (conn, ix) {">
							<outline text="if (conn.appData !== undefined) { //it's one of ours">
								<outline text="theArray.push ({">
									<outline text="arrayIndex: ix,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="lastVerb: conn.appData.lastVerb,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="urlToWatch: conn.appData.urlToWatch,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="domain: conn.appData.domain,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="whenStarted: utils.viewDate (conn.appData.whenStarted),">
									</outline>
									<outline text="whenLastUpdate: utils.viewDate (conn.appData.whenLastUpdate)">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="return (theArray);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="" isComment="true">
						</outline>
						<outline text="for (var i = 0; i &lt; theWsServer.clients.length; i++) {" isComment="true">
							<outline text="var conn = theWsServer.clients [i];">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (conn.chatLogData !== undefined) { //it's one of ours">
								<outline text="theArray [theArray.length] = {">
									<outline text="arrayIndex: i,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="lastVerb: conn.chatLogData.lastVerb,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="urlToWatch: conn.chatLogData.urlToWatch,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="domain: conn.chatLogData.domain,">
									</outline>
									<outline text="whenStarted: utils.viewDate (conn.chatLogData.whenStarted),">
									</outline>
									<outline text="whenLastUpdate: utils.viewDate (conn.chatLogData.whenLastUpdate)">
									</outline>
									<outline text="};">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function handleWebSocketConnection (conn) { ">
						<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
							<outline text="2/23/25; 6:37:46 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Make sure conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo is not undefined.">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="5/24/24; 5:25:44 PM by DW">
								<outline text="Ported from daveappserver.">
								</outline>
								<outline text="There's a struct at conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo that has this info in it.">
									<outline text="{">
										<outline text="&quot;idUser&quot;: 21807,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Dave Winer&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;username&quot;: &quot;scripting&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;email&quot;: &quot;dave@scripting.com&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;idPrimaryBlog&quot;: 9969399,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;urlPrimaryBlog&quot;: &quot;http://unberkeley.wordpress.com&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;whenStarted&quot;: &quot;2005-11-21T15:45:53.000Z&quot;,">
										</outline>
										<outline text="&quot;ctSites&quot;: 32">
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="var now = new Date ();">
						</outline>
						<outline text="console.log (&quot;handleWebSocketConnection&quot;);">
						</outline>
						<outline text="conn.appData = { //initialize">
							<outline text="whenStarted: now,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="ctUpdates: 0,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="whenLastUpdate: new Date (0),">
							</outline>
							<outline text="lastVerb: undefined,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="urlToWatch: undefined,">
							</outline>
							<outline text="domain: undefined">
							</outline>
							<outline text="};">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="function logToConsole (conn, verb, value) {">
							<outline text="getDomainName (conn.socket.remoteAddress, function (theName) { //log the request" isComment="true">
								<outline text="var freemem = utils.gigabyteString (os.freemem ()), method = &quot;WS:&quot; + verb, now = new Date (); ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="if (theName === undefined) {">
									<outline text="theName = conn.socket.remoteAddress;">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (now.toLocaleTimeString () + &quot; &quot; + freemem + &quot; &quot; + method + &quot; &quot; + value + &quot; &quot; + theName);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="conn.appData.domain = theName; ">
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="function kissOtherLogonsGoodnight (username, theNewConnection) {">
							<outline text="Changes" isComment="true">
								<outline text="12/14/21; 5:21:51 PM by DW">
									<outline text="Loop over the other instances with the same screenname, and tell them to have a good night. ">
									</outline>
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="theWsServer.clients.forEach (function (conn, ix) {">
								<outline text="if (conn.appData !== undefined) { //it's one of ours">
									<outline text="if (conn != theNewConnection) { //it's not the new one">
										<outline text="if (conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo !== undefined) { //2/23/25 by DW">
											<outline text="if (conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo.username == username) {">
												<outline text="console.log (&quot;kissOtherLogonsGoodnight: \&quot;&quot; + conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo.username + &quot;\&quot; = \&quot;&quot; + username + &quot;\&quot;&quot;); ">
												</outline>
												<outline text="conn.send (&quot;goodnight&quot;);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="}">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="});">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="}">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="">
						</outline>
						<outline text="conn.on (&quot;message&quot;, function (theMessage) {">
							<outline text="const s = theMessage.toString ();">
							</outline>
							<outline text="var words = s.split (&quot; &quot;);">
							</outline>
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;handleWebSocketConnection: s == &quot; + s); //6/7/21 by DW" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="if (words.length &gt; 1) { //new protocol as of 11/29/15 by DW">
								<outline text="conn.appData.whenLastUpdate = now;">
								</outline>
								<outline text="conn.appData.lastVerb = words [0];">
								</outline>
								<outline text="switch (words [0]) {">
									<outline text="case &quot;greetings&quot;: ">
										<outline text="let accessToken = utils.trimWhitespace (words [1]);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="getUserInfo (accessToken, function (err, theUserInfo) {">
											<outline text="if (!err) {">
												<outline text="conn.appData.accessToken = accessToken;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="conn.appData.wordpressUserInfo = theUserInfo;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="console.log (&quot;handleWebSocketConnection: conn.appData == &quot; + utils.jsonStringify (conn.appData));">
												</outline>
												<outline text="">
												</outline>
												<outline text="const eventData = { //12/21/24 by DW">
													<outline text="email: theUserInfo.email, ">
													</outline>
													<outline text="name: theUserInfo.name, ">
													</outline>
													<outline text="username: theUserInfo.username">
													</outline>
													<outline text="{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Dave Winer&quot;, &quot;email&quot;: &quot;dave@scripting.com&quot;, &quot;idUser&quot;: 21807, &quot;ctSites&quot;: 34, &quot;username&quot;: &quot;scripting&quot;, &quot;whenStarted&quot;: &quot;2005-11-21T15:45:53.000Z&quot;, &quot;idPrimaryBlog&quot;: 9969399, &quot;urlPrimaryBlog&quot;: &quot;http://unberkeley.wordpress.com&quot;}" isComment="true">
													</outline>
													<outline text="}">
													</outline>
												</outline>
												<outline text="addToLog (&quot;connect&quot;, undefined, eventData);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="">
												</outline>
												<outline text="kissOtherLogonsGoodnight (theUserInfo.username, conn);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="}">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="});">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="break;">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="case &quot;watch&quot;:" isComment="true">
										<outline text="conn.appData.urlToWatch = utils.trimWhitespace (words [1]);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="logToConsole (conn, conn.appData.lastVerb, conn.appData.urlToWatch);">
										</outline>
										<outline text="break;">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="case &quot;user&quot;: //9/29/21 by DW" isComment="true">
										<outline text="if (config.flUseTwitterIdentity) { //2/12/23 by DW">
											<outline text="var token = words [1], secret = words [2];">
											</outline>
											<outline text="conn.appData.twOauthToken = token;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="conn.appData.twOauthTokenSecret = secret;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="conn.appData.urlToWatch = &quot;&quot;;">
											</outline>
											<outline text="davetwitter.getScreenName (token, secret, function (screenname) {">
												<outline text="conn.appData.screenname = screenname;">
												</outline>
												<outline text="kissOtherLogonsGoodnight (screenname, conn); //12/14/21 by DW">
												</outline>
												<outline text="logToConsole (conn, conn.appData.lastVerb, conn.appData.screenname);">
												</outline>
												<outline text="});">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="else {">
											<outline text="var emailAddress = words [1], emailSecret = words [2];">
											</outline>
											<outline text="config.findUserWithEmail (emailAddress, function (flInDatabase, userRec) {">
												<outline text="if (flInDatabase) {">
													<outline text="conn.appData.emailAddress = userRec.emailAddress;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="conn.appData.screenname = userRec.emailAddress;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="conn.appData.emailSecret = userRec.emailSecret;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="conn.appData.urlToWatch = &quot;&quot;;">
													</outline>
													<outline text="kissOtherLogonsGoodnight (conn.appData.screenname, conn); ">
													</outline>
													<outline text="logToConsole (conn, conn.appData.lastVerb, conn.appData.screenname);">
													</outline>
													<outline text="}">
													</outline>
												</outline>
												<outline text="});">
												</outline>
											</outline>
											<outline text="}">
											</outline>
										</outline>
										<outline text="break;">
										</outline>
									</outline>
									<outline text="">
									</outline>
									<outline text="}">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="else {">
								<outline text="conn.close ();">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="conn.on (&quot;close&quot;, function () {">
							<outline text="console.log (&quot;'close' message received.&quot;);" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="conn.on (&quot;error&quot;, function (err) {">
							<outline text="logToConsole (conn, &quot;error&quot;, err.code);" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="conn.close (); //11/30/15 by DW -- https://github.com/scripting/betterWebSocketsDemo/issues/2#issuecomment-160658118" isComment="true">
							</outline>
							<outline text="});">
							</outline>
						</outline>
						<outline text="}">
						</outline>
					</outline>
					<outline text="function webSocketStartup () {">
						<outline text="if (config.flWebsocketEnabled) {">
							<outline text="try {">
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;webSocketStartup: config.websocketPort == &quot; + config.websocketPort);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theWsServer = new websocket.Server ({port: config.websocketPort});">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theWsServer.on (&quot;connection&quot;, handleWebSocketConnection);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="theWsServer.on (&quot;error&quot;, function (err) {">
									<outline text="console.log (&quot;webSocketStartup: server error == &quot; + err.message);">
									</outline>
									<outline text="});">
									</outline>
								</outline>
								<outline text="console.log (&quot;webSocketStartup: websocket server successfully listening on port &quot; + config.websocketPort);">
								</outline>
								<outline text="}">
								</outline>
							</outline>
							<outline text="catch (err) {">
